    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Painting and filling"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "To paint a water tank you need its surface area. To fill it you need its volume. Both depend on its shape."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "cone",
          "cone volume",
          "cuboid",
          "cylinder volume",
          "slant height",
          "sphere",
          "total surface area",
          "units"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A cuboid with length l, width w and height h has surface area 2(wl + hw + lh) and volume whl.\nA right circular cylinder has curved surface area 2 pi r h and volume pi r^2 h.\nThe total surface area of a cylinder closed at both ends is 2 pi r (h + r).\nA right circular cone has curved surface area pi r l, where l is the slant height, and total surface area pi r (l + r).\nThe volume of a cone is one third pi r^2 h, exactly one third of the cylinder with the same base and height.\nA sphere has surface area 4 pi r^2 and volume four thirds pi r^3.\nThe slant height of a cone satisfies l^2 = r^2 + h^2.\nSurface area is measured in square units and volume in cubic units."
        }
      },
